hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"260","Wa qāla ṣallā Allāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam: Yā ʿAbdallāh ibn Qays, a-lā adulluka ʿalā kanzin min kunūz al-jannati? Fa-qultu: balā yā Rasūl Allāh, qāla: qul (lā ḥawla wa-lā quwwata illā billāh).. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: \O Abdullah ibn Qays"," shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise?\"" I said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""Say: 'There is no power and no strength except with Allah (lā ḥawla wa-lā quwwata illā billāh).'\"""""
"261","The most beloved words to Allah are four: Subḥānallāh Walḥamdu lillāh. Wa lā ilāha illallāh Wallāhu Akbar. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: The most beloved words to Allah are four: Glorified is Allah, and The praise is for Allah, and There is none worthy of worship but Allah, and Allah is the Most Great. Reference: Muslim 3/1685."
